      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Parameters",
      "contextAfter": "`context`: A pointer to the structure into which the context information for `s` is to be copied. The information being returned is usually the same information you passed to [`CFSocketCreate(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](cfsocketcreate(_:_:_:_:_:_:_:).md), [`CFSocketCreateConnectedToSocketSignature(_:_:_:_:_:_:)`](cfsocketcreateconnectedtosocketsignature(_:_:_:_:_:_:).md), [`CFSocketCreateWithNative(_:_:_:_:_:)`](cfsocketcreatewithnative(_:_:_:_:_:).md), or [`CFSocketCreateWithSocketSignature(_:_:_:_:_:)`](cfsocketcreatewithsocketsignature(_:_:_:_:_:).md) when creating the CFSocket object. However, if [`CFSocketCreateWithNative(_:_:_:_:_:)`](cfsocketcreatewithnative(_:_:_:_:_:).md) returned a cached CFSocket object instead of creating a new object, `context` is filled with information from the original CFSocket object instead of the information you passed to the function.",
